 System L49:       * cite12†Understanding the eCFR L50:       * cite13†Government Policy and OFR Procedures L51:       * cite14†Developer Resources L52:       * cite15†Recent Site Updates L53:     * My eCFR\nL54:       * cite16†Sign In / Sign Up L55:     * [Input] [Input: Search the eCFR]\nL56: # cite1†eCFR L57: \nL58: ## The Electronic Code of Federal Regulations\nL59: \nL60: ###### Enhanced Content :: FR Reference\nL61: \nL62: Enhanced content is provided to the user to provide additional context.\nL63: \nL64: ###### Enhanced Content :: FR Reference\nL65: # Title 47\nL66: \nL67: This content is from the eCFR and is authoritative but unofficial.\nL68: \nL69: Displaying title 47, up to date as of 9/24/2026. Title 47 was last amended 9/22/2026.\nL70: \nL71: cite0†view historical versions L72: \nL73: A cite17†drafting site is available†drafting.ecfr.gov for use when drafting amendatory language\nL74: \nL75: cite17†switch to drafting site†drafting.ecfr.gov L76: \nL77: Navigate by entering citations or phrases (eg: 1 CFR 1.1 49 CFR 172.101 Organization and Purpose 1/1.1 Regulation Y FAR).\nL78: Choosing an item from citations and headings will bring you directly to the content. Choosing an item from full text search results will bring you to those results. Pressing enter in the search box will also bring you to search results.\nL79: \nL80: Background and more details are available in the cite18†Search & Navigation guide.\nL81: \nL82: [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL83: \nL84: [Input: Enter a search term or CFR reference (eg. fishing or 1 CFR 1.1)]\nL85: \nL86: [Input: Enter a search term or CFR reference (eg. fishing or 1 CFR 1.1)]\nL87:   *   * Table of Contents\nL88:   * Details\nL89:   * Print/PDF\nL90:   * Display Options\nL91:   *   * Timeline\nL92:   * Go to Date\nL93:   * Compare Dates\nL94:   *   * Published Edition\nL95:   *   * Developer Tools\nL96: ###### eCFR Content\nL97: \nL98: The Code of Federal Regulations (CFR) is the official legal print publication containing the codification of the general and permanent rules published in the Federal Register by the departments and agencies of the Federal Government. The Electronic Code of Federal Regulations (eCFR) is a continuously updated online version of the CFR. It is not an official legal edition of the CFR.\nL99: \nL100: cite19†Learn more about the eCFR, its status, and the editorial process.\nL101: ###### Enhanced Content\nL102: \nL103: View table of contents for this page.\nL104: \nL105: ## Subpart T—Notices\nL106: \nL107: #### Source:\nL108: \nL109: cite20†65 FR 53617†www.federalregister.gov , Sept. 5, 2000, unless otherwise noted.\nL110: #### § 76.1600 Electronic delivery of notices.\nL111: (a) Except as provided in cite21†§ 76.1603 for changes that occur due to circumstances outside a cable operator's control, which also may be provided as set forth in 76.1603(b), written information provided by cable operators to subscribers or customers pursuant to cite22†§§ 76.1601 , cite23†76.1602 , cite24†76.1603 , cite25†76.1604 , cite26†76.1618 , and cite27†76.1620 of this subpart T, as well as subscriber privacy notifications required by cable operators, satellite providers, and open video systems pursuant to sections 631, 338(i), and 653 of the Communications Act, may be delivered electronically by email to any subscriber who has not opted out of electronic delivery under cite28†paragraph (a)(3) of this section if the entity:\nL112: (1) Sends the notice to the subscriber's or customer's verified email address;\nL113: \nL114: (2) Provides either the entirety of the written information or a weblink to the written information in the notice; and\nL115: \nL116: (3) Includes, in the body of the notice, a telephone number that is clearly and prominently presented to subscribers so that it is readily identifiable as an opt-out mechanism that will allow subscribers to continue to receive paper copies of the written material.\nL117: (b) For purposes of this section, a verified email address is defined as:\nL118: \nL119: (1) An email address that the subscriber has provided to the cable operator (and not vice versa) for purposes of receiving communication;\nL120: \nL121: (2) An email address that the subscriber regularly uses to communicate with the cable operator; or\nL122: \nL123: (3) An email address that has been confirmed by the subscriber as an appropriate vehicle for the delivery of notices.\nL124: (c) Cable operators that provide written Subpart T notices via paper copy may provide certain portions of the cite29†§ 76.1602 annual notices electronically, to any subscriber who has not opted out of electronic delivery under cite28†paragraphs (a)(3) or cite30†(c)(3) of this section, by prominently displaying the following on the front or first page of the printed annual notice:\nL125: (1) A weblink in a form that is short, simple, and easy to remember, leading to written information required to be provided pursuant to cite31†§ 76.1602(b)(2) , cite32†(7) , and cite33†(8) ;\nL126: \nL127: (2) A weblink in a form that is short, simple, and easy to remember, leading to written information required to be provided pursuant to cite34†§ 76.1602(b)(5) ; and\nL128: (3) A telephone number that is readily identifiable as an opt-out mechanism that will allow subscribers to continue to receive paper copies of the entire annual notice.\nL129: \nL130: (d) If the conditions for electronic delivery in cite35†paragraphs (a) and cite36†(b) of this section are not met, or if a subscriber opts out of electronic delivery, the written material must be delivered by paper copy to the subscriber's physical address.\nL131: (e) After July 31, 2020, written information provided by cable operators to broadcast stations pursuant to cite37†§§ 76.64(k) , cite38†76.1601 , cite39†76.1607 , cite40†76.1608 , cite41†76.1609 , and cite42†76.1617 must be delivered electronically to full-power and Class A television stations via email to the email address for carriage-related questions that the station lists in its public file in accordance with cite43†§§ 73.3526 and cite44†73.3527 of this title , or in the case of low power television stations and noncommercial educational translator stations that are entitled to such notices, to the licensee's email address (not a contact representative's email address, if different from the licensee's email address) as displayed publicly in the Licensing and Management System (LMS) or the primary station's carriage-related email address if the noncommercial educational translator station does not have its own email address listed in LMS.\nL132: [cite45†83 FR 66157†www.federalregister.gov , Dec. 26, 2019, as amended at cite46†85 FR 16005†www.federalregister.gov , Mar. 20, 2020; cite47†85 FR 71854†www.federalregister.gov , Nov. 12, 2020]\nL133: #### § 76.1601 Deletion or repositioning of broadcast signals.\nL134: \nL135: A cable operator shall provide written notice to any broadcast television station at least 30 days prior to either deleting from carriage or repositioning that station.\nL136: \nL137: [cite47†85 FR 71854†www.federalregister.gov , Nov. 12, 2020]\nL138: #### § 76.1602 Customer service—general information.\nL139: \nL140: (a) A cable franchise authority may enforce the customer service standards set forth in cite48†paragraph (b) of this section against cable operators. The franchise authority must provide affected cable operators 90 days written notice of its intent to enforce standards.\nL141: (b) The cable operator shall provide written information on each of the following areas at the time of installation of service, at least annually to all subscribers, and at any time upon request:\nL142: \nL143: (1) Products and services offered;\nL144: \nL145: (2) Prices and options for programming services and conditions of subscription to programming and other services;\nL146: \nL147: (3) Installation and service maintenance policies;\nL148: \nL149: (4) Instructions on how to use the cable service;\nL150: (5) Channel positions of programming carried on the system; and\nL151: \nL152: (6) Billing and complaint procedures, including the address and telephone number of the local franchise authority's cable office.\nL153: \nL154: (7) Effective May 1, 2011, any assessed fees for rental of navigation devices and single and additional CableCARDs; and,\nL155: \nL156: (8) Effective May 1, 2011, if such provider includes equipment in the price of a bundled offer of one or more services, the fees reasonably allocable to:\nL157: (i) The rental of single and additional CableCARDs; and\nL158: \nL159: (ii) The rental of operator-supplied navigation devices.\nL160: \nL161: (c) Subscribers shall be advised of the procedures for resolution of complaints about the quality of the television signal delivered by the cable system operator, including the address of the responsible officer of the local franchising authority.\nL162: [cite20†65 FR 53617†www.federalregister.gov , Sept. 5, 2000, as amended at cite49†76 FR 40279†www.federalregister.gov , July 8, 2011; cite50†83 FR 7631†www.federalregister.gov , Feb. 22, 2018]\nL163: #### § 76.1603 Customer service—rate and service changes.\nL164: \nL165: (a) A cable franchise authority may enforce the customer service standards set forth in cite51†paragraph (b) of this section against cable operators. The franchise authority must provide affected cable operators 90 days written notice of its intent to enforce standards.\nL166: (b) Cable operators shall provide written notice to subscribers of any changes in rates or services.\nL167: Notice shall be provided to subscribers at least 30 days in advance of the change, unless the change results from circumstances outside of the cable operator's control (including failed retransmission consent or program carriage negotiations during the last 30 days of a contract), in which case notice shall be provided as soon as possible using any reasonable written means at the operator's sole discretion, including Channel Slates.\nL168: Notice of rate changes shall include the precise amount of the rate change and explain the reason for the change in readily understandable terms. Notice of changes involving the addition or deletion of channels shall individually identify each channel affected.\nL169: (c) A cable operator not subject to effective competition shall provide 30 days' advance notice to its local franchising authority of any increase proposed in the price to be charged for the basic service tier.\nL170: (d) Notwithstanding any other provision of cite52†part 76 of this chapter , a cable operator shall not be required to provide prior notice of any rate change that is the result of a regulatory fee, franchise fee, or any other fee, tax, assessment, or charge of any kind imposed by any Federal agency, State, or franchising authority on the transaction between the operator and the subscriber.\nL171: \nL172: Note 1 to cite21†§ 76.1603 :\nL173: Section 624(h) of the Communications Act, cite53†47 U.S.C. 544(h)†www.govinfo.gov , contains additional notification requirements which a franchising authority may enforce.\nL174: \nL175: Note 2 to cite21†§ 76.1603 :\nL176: \nL177: Section 624(d)(3) of the Communications Act, cite53†47 U.S.C. 544(d)(3)†www.govinfo.gov , contains additional notification provisions pertaining to cable operators who offer a premium channel without charge to cable subscribers who do not subscribe to such premium channel.\nL178: \nL179: Note 3 to cite21†§ 76.1603 :\nL180: Section 631 of the Communications Act, cite54†47 U.S.C. 551†www.govinfo.gov , contains additional notification requirements pertaining to the protection of subscriber privacy.\nL181: \nL182: [cite20†65 FR 53617†www.federalregister.gov , Sept. 5, 2000, as amended at cite55†66 FR 16554†www.federalregister.gov , Mar. 26, 2001; cite56†77 FR 67302†www.federalregister.gov , Dec. 10, 2012; cite47†85 FR 71854†www.federalregister.gov , Nov. 12, 2020]\nL183: #### § 76.1604 Charges for customer service changes.\nL184: \nL185: If a cable operator establishes a higher charge for changes effected solely by coded entry on a computer terminal or by other similarly simple methods, as provided in cite57†§ 76.980(d) , the cable system must notify all subscribers in writing that they may be subject to such a charge for changing service tiers more than the specified number of times in any 12 month period.\nL186: #### § 76.1607 Principal headend.\nL187: \nL188: A cable operator shall provide written notice to all stations carried on its system pursuant to the must-carry rules in this subpart at least 60 days prior to any change in the designation of its principal headend. Such written notice shall be provided by certified mail, except that after July 31, 2020, notice shall be provided to stations by electronic delivery in accordance with cite58†§ 76.1600 .\nL189: \nL190: [cite59†85 FR 16006†www.federalregister.gov , Mar. 20, 2020]\nL191: #### § 76.1608 System technical integration requiring uniform election of must-carry or retransmission consent status.\nL192: A cable system that changes its technical configuration in such a way as to integrate two formerly separate cable systems must give 90 days notice of its intention to do so to any television broadcast stations that have elected must-carry status with respect to one system and retransmission consent status with respect to the other. After July 31, 2020, such notice shall be delivered to stations electronically in accordance with cite58†§ 76.1600 .\nL193: If the system and the station do not agree on a uniform election 45 days prior to integration, the cable system may require the station to make such a uniform election 30 days prior to integration.\nL194: [cite59†85 FR 16006†www.federalregister.gov , Mar. 20, 2020]\nL195: #### § 76.1609 Non-duplication and syndicated exclusivity.\nL196: Within 60 days following the provision of service to 1,000 subscribers, the operator of each such system shall file a notice to that effect with the Commission, and serve a copy of that notice on every television station that would be entitled to exercise network non-duplication protection or syndicated exclusivity protection against it.\nL197: After July 31, 2020, in lieu of serving paper copies on stations, the operator shall provide the required copies to stations by electronic delivery in accordance with cite58†§ 76.1600 .\nL198: [cite59†85 FR 16006†www.federalregister.gov , Mar. 20, 2020]\nL199: #### § 76.1610 Change of operational information.\nL200: \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn2420view2 [wordlim: 200] Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn2410view0\",\"id\":18}); Total lines: 1\n"
